//@version=5
// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// © reees
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// MODIFIED WORK — enhancement layer added on top of reees' original.
// Original: "Harmonic Pattern Detection, Prediction, and Backtesting System"
// © reees, licensed MPL-2.0. This file remains under MPL-2.0.
//
// All detection, scoring, drawing and statistics logic below is reees' work and
// is UNCHANGED. Every addition is fenced in "ENH:" blocks and every one of them
// defaults OFF or is display-only, so with default settings this script behaves
// identically to the original. Turn things on deliberately.
//
// WHAT IS ADDED, AND WHY
//   1. MINIMUM R:R GATE. The original has no reward:risk filter anywhere — a
//      0.5:1 setup is entered on the same terms as a 3:1. Given the original's
//      own published stats (T1 success around 50%, T2 around 20%), filtering on
//      R:R is the single highest-leverage addition. Computed from pattern
//      geometry alone, so it is deterministic for a given pattern.
//   2. HIGHER-TIMEFRAME BIAS. Optionally suppress counter-trend patterns.
//      Applied once at discovery in find(), never re-evaluated, so a pattern
//      cannot pass and later fail.
//   3. POSITION SIZING. Shows the actual unit/lot size for a chosen account
//      risk %, instead of leaving it to be worked out by hand.
//   4. EDGE METRICS. Profit factor, expectancy per trade, and worst losing
//      streak. The original reports return % but not the metrics that answer
//      "is there an edge here" — a positive total return with PF below 1.3 and
//      a 9-trade losing streak is not a tradeable system.
//   5. LIVE PANEL. The original's stats table is entirely historical, yet its
//      `pending` and `inc` arrays already hold exactly what is actionable right
//      now. This surfaces them: setups awaiting D, and open trades with current R.
//
// IMPLEMENTATION NOTE. The R:R filter calls t.harmonic_xabcd_entry() directly
// rather than the script's own entry() wrapper. entry() calls noEntry(), so
// routing through it from inside noEntry() would be infinite recursion, which
// Pine forbids.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

indicator("Harmonic Pattern Detection, Prediction, and Backtesting System [enhanced]","Harmonics+",overlay=true,max_lines_count=500,max_labels_count=500,max_bars_back=500)

import reees/TA/85 as t
import reees/Draw/27 as draw
import reees/Utilities/5 as u
import reees/Pattern/1 as p
import reees/Obj_XABCD_Harmonic/10 as h

//----------------------------------------- 
// inputs and vars  
